Subject: Do not enumerate libc collations with "locale -a" in a shell-less image
Purpose: initdb's pg_import_system_collations() runs "locale -a" through a pipe. The scratch image has neither a shell nor a locale program, and a WebAssembly module has no processes at all, so initdb died after bootstrap with "could not execute command locale -a". With PG_NO_SHELL the libc enumeration is not compiled in; the builtin collations from pg_collation.dat (C, C.UTF-8, ucs_basic) are created as usual and are the ones the profile uses. Without PG_NO_SHELL the code is upstream's.
Components: src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
Checks: ./dcb musl make native-test / scripts/native-image.sh test 18.6: cold initdb in the scratch image completes and SELECT collname FROM pg_collation lists the builtin collations
Origin: own

diff --git a/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c b/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
index 8acbfbb..0d1e4ba 100644
--- a/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
+++ b/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
@@ -574,8 +574,14 @@ pg_collation_actual_version(PG_FUNCTION_ARGS)
 }
 
 
-/* will we use "locale -a" in pg_import_system_collations? */
-#if !defined(WIN32)
+/*
+ * will we use "locale -a" in pg_import_system_collations?
+ *
+ * Not in an image without a shell and without a "locale" program (PG_NO_SHELL):
+ * the libc collations cannot be enumerated there, and the builtin ones (C, C.UTF-8,
+ * ucs_basic, from pg_collation.dat) are what the server uses.
+ */
+#if !defined(WIN32) && !defined(PG_NO_SHELL)
 #define READ_LOCALE_A_OUTPUT
 #endif
 
